  "lineage": "The model works promoted during the Cultural Revolution (1966-1976), led by revolutionary modern Peking operas such as The Red Lantern, Shajiabang and Taking Tiger Mountain by Strategy, alongside the ballets The Red Detachment of Women and The White-Haired Girl. Jingju singing and gong-and-drum percussion were set against a combined orchestra in which the jinghu, jing erhu and yueqin played beside Western strings, horns and timpani.",
